Package: koken
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         python3-pyside6.qtcore,
         python3-pyside6.qtgui,
         python3-pyside6.qtwidgets,
         python3-pyside6.qtdbus,
         hwdata,
         udisks2,
         dmidecode,
         pkexec
Suggests: smartmontools
Description: Machine Corpus - a hardware and system browser that explains itself
 KOKEN reads what this machine is made of and says, in plain language, what
 each value means and why it might matter. It is offline and read-only: it
 opens no network connection of any kind.
 .
 Every row carries an explanation you can open in place, covering the values
 people actually stop and look at - PCIe link width, memory channel
 configuration, SMART health, battery wear, processor vulnerability status,
 Secure Boot and kernel lockdown.
 .
 Debian ships PySide6 split into one binary package per Qt module, which is why
 four of them are named here rather than one. That is expected, not a mistake.
 .
 pkexec rather than policykit-1: the policykit-1 binary package was transitional
 in bookworm and does not exist in trixie at all. Its source package now builds
 pkexec and polkitd, and pkexec depends on polkitd, so naming pkexec brings both.
 .
 smartmontools is Suggests and deliberately not Recommends. Policy reserves
 Recommends for a package that would be found alongside this one in all but
 unusual installations, and apt installs Recommends by default - so choosing it
 would put smartd, a monitoring daemon with a systemd unit that starts at boot
 and mails root, onto every machine that installs a read-only browser. That is
 a change to how the machine behaves, made on the user's behalf, to add one
 table to one tab. Without smartmontools the Storage branch keeps its SMART
 health verdict, temperature, power-on hours, bad sector count and self-test
 result, all of them from udisks2 over D-Bus; what is lost is the per-attribute
 table, which is the one thing udisks2 returns in a form the Qt binding cannot
 read. That is an enhancement to one section, which is precisely Suggests.
